    "title": "More humidity by the weekend - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Hank Allen ,\n34 minutes ago\nNEW ORLEANS ( WGNO ) — A big bubble of high pressure sitting over eastern Texas is running the show right now, keeping us warm, dry, and mostly sunny. Humidity is still on the low side, so nights will feel nice and comfortable, with lows in the upper 50s to around 60. This setup sticks around through Thursday before that high starts sliding east. Once it does, winds will turn off the Gulf again, and we’ll start to see a little more moisture creeping back in.\nFriday looks a lot like what we’ve had lately — warm, dry, and pleasant. But heading into the weekend, we’ll start to notice some changes. A weak disturbance will move across the region late Saturday into Sunday, and that could spark a few showers or storms, mainly north of I-10 and I-12. Most of the stronger stuff should stay up toward the ArkLaTex, but we’ll keep tabs on it just in case things shift closer to us.\nAfter that, it’s back to quiet weather for next week. We’ll warm up a bit with higher humidity as those southerly winds hang around, but overall, it’s looking like another stretch of mild, easygoing weather for mid-October.\nStay up to date with the latest news, weather and sports by downloading the WGNO app on the Apple or Google Play stores and by subscribing to the WGNO newsletter .\nLatest Posts More humidity by the weekend Suspect evades capture in Marrero car chase, community on alert New Orleans Mayor-Elect Helena Moreno announces transition team Fatal shooting in Slidell Pop musician Carnie Wilson talks mental, physical health Copyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WGNO.",
